    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "BACKGROUND",
      "narration_text": "Midjourney's own guide says it plainly: every image begins as random noise, like the static on an old TV. That starting noise comes from a number called a seed. From there, the model does one thing, over and over. It looks at the static, and removes a little of the noise. Do that enough times, and a picture is left.",
